.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH SPT-UPDATE 1  "update " 
.SH NAME
update \- Embedded auto\-updater (off by default). Manual commands work regardless of the `[updater].enabled` flag; the background polling thread is only spawned when explicitly enabled
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBupdate\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Embedded auto\-updater (off by default). Manual commands work regardless of the `[updater].enabled` flag; the background polling thread is only spawned when explicitly enabled
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
update\-check(1)
One\-shot poll: print whether a newer release is available
.TP
update\-download(1)
Download the latest artifact to the staging directory without installing
.TP
update\-apply(1)
Install the staged artifact (atomic swap, then optional restart)
.TP
update\-now(1)
Run `check` + `download` + `apply` in one go
.TP
update\-status(1)
Print current status: enabled flag, last check, latest version, next\-scheduled tick, staged artifact
.TP
update\-history(1)
Past update events from the audit log
.TP
update\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
